  <data name="Skin_Readme" xml:space="preserve"><value>Desktop Pet — Skins Folder
========================

Each skin is one folder here:

  Skins\&lt;SkinName&gt;\spritesheet.png   (required, RGBA PNG with transparency)
  Skins\&lt;SkinName&gt;\skin.json         (optional, see skin.example.json)

Atlas contract (same as Codex v2 pets):
  - 8 columns x 11 rows of cells. Default: 192 x 208 px cells, 1536 x 2288 px atlas.
  - Rows 0-8 : idle, running-right, running-left, waving, jumping, failed, waiting, running, review
  - Rows 9-10: 16 gaze directions (0 degrees = up, clockwise, 22.5 degree steps)

skin.json may change the cell size, frame count (1-8), per-frame duration (40-2000 ms), and loop.
The row order cannot be changed. waving and jumping always play once.

Codex pets (spritesheet.webp) must be converted to PNG first, because the built-in
Windows WebP decoder drops transparency. Use:
  powershell -File scripts\import-codex-pet.ps1 -Name &lt;pet-name&gt;

After adding a folder, pick the skin in the Control Panel ("Reload List" button)
or right-click the pet &gt; Skin. No restart needed.
</value></data>
  <data name="Skin_ExampleManifest" xml:space="preserve"><value>{
  // Copy this file to Skins\&lt;SkinName&gt;\skin.json and adjust it.
  "name": "Skin Name",
  "author": "Your Name",
  "description": "Short description",
  "spritesheet": "spritesheet.png",
  "cellWidth": 192,
  "cellHeight": 208,
  "animations": {
    "idle":    { "frames": 6, "durations": [280, 110, 110, 140, 140, 320] },
    "running": { "durations": [120, 120, 120, 120, 120, 220] }
  }
}
</value></data>

